          |\r\n|   Notify                    | > Preview Fit: On                                                  |\r\n|                             |     Kind: toggle · Scope: global                                   |\r\n|                             |     When true, the passive preview fits the selected session's     |\r\n|                             |     window to the preview panel as the list selection settles --   |\r\n|                             |     coalesced against the 250ms preview tick, skipped below the    |\r\n|                             |     7-inner-row interactive floor, and best-effort (owning and     |\r\n|                             |     restoring nothing; an attaching client's own size simply wins) |\r\n|                             |     -- rather than leaving a session cropped bottom-left at wha... |\r\n|                             |     size it last had (SPEC §11). The cost: a fit sends the agent   |\r\n|                             |     SIGWINCH and reflows its output, so output produced while n... |\r\n|                             |     consumes scrollback rows faster and evicted rows never return. |\r\n|                             |     false restores a wholly passive preview -- capture-pane -e ... |\r\n|                             |     no resize, cropped bottom-left. On by default. DECK_PREVIEW... |\r\n|                             |     overrides the file when set.                                   |\r\n|                             |   Recent Cwd Limit: 5 entries (0-50)                               |\r\n|                             |   Group By Workspace: On                                           |\r\n|                             |   Sort Order: attention                                            |\r\n|                             |   Clear Recent Cwds: press enter/space to clear now                |\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\x1b[30;H\x1b[H\n\n\n\n|   Notify                    |   Preview Fit: On                                                  |\r\n|                             | > Recent Cwd Limit: 5 entries (0-50)                               |\r\n|                             |     Kind: integer · Scope: restart-to-apply                        |\r\n|                             |     The number of recently used working directories offered when   |\r\n|                             |     creating a session (SPEC §11.7). The recent-directory list     |\r\n|                             |     itself lives in state.db, not config.toml — this key only b... |\r\n|                             |     how many entries are kept/offered. Restart-to-apply: saving... |\r\n|                             |     writes config.toml immediately, but nothing in the             |\r\n|                             |     already-running client reads it again until deck restarts.     |\r\n|                             |   Group By Workspace: On                                           |\r\n|                             |   Sort Order: attention                                            |\r\n|                             |   Clear Recent Cwds: press enter/space to clear now                |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\x1b[30;H\x1b[H\n\n\n\n\n|                             |   Recent Cwd Limit: 5 entries (0-50)                               |\r\n|                             | > Group By Workspace: On                                           |\r\n|                             |     Kind: toggle · Scope: restart-to-apply                         |\r\n|                             |     Groups the sidebar by sessions.workspace, defaulting to the    |\r\n|                             |     basename of cwd, with each group's own collapsed/expanded s... |\r\n|                             |     (`c`) preserved (SPEC §11/requirement 30). On by default; o... |\r\n|                             |     an explicit opt-out for a flat, ungrouped sidebar.             |\r\n|                             |   Sort Order: attention                                            |\r\n|                             |   Clear Recent Cwds: press enter/space to clear now                |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n|                             |                                                                    |\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\x1b[30;H\x1b[H\n\n\n\n\n\n|                             |   Group By Workspace: On                                           |\r\n|                             | > Sort Order: attention                                            |\r\n|                             |     Kind: enum · Scope: global                                     |\r\n|                             |     Orders the sidebar (SPEC §11, amendment 6584299). \"attention\"  |\r\n|                             |     (default) is the unchanged                                     |\r\n|                             |     waiting/error/running/starting/idle/stopped tier order -- the  |\r\n|                             |     order every earlier phase shipped, kept default because it     |\r\n|                             |     answers \"which session needs me\". \"created\" is                 |\r\n|                             |     sessions.created_at descending (newest first). \"activity\" is   |\r\n|                             |     sessions.status_at descending -- a status CHANGE (§7's own     |\r\n|                             |     timestamp), never last pane output, which deck does not rec... |\r\n|                             |     \"name\" is case-insensitive ascending. Every order falls bac... |\r\n|                             |     id ascending on a tie (a total order, so a re-sort can never   |\r\n|                             |     swap two rows out from under an in-flight keyboard idiom), ... |\r\n|                             |     non-attention order never secretly re-ranks by status --       |\r\n|                             |     choosing one means the user, not deck, decides what \"first\"    |\r\n|                             |     means. An unknown/malformed value falls back to attention and  |\r\n|                             |     says so on the first painted frame, never silently.            |\r\n|                             |   Clear Recent Cwds: press enter/space to clear now                |\r\n\n\n\n\n\x1b[30;H\x1b[H\n\n\n\n\n\n\n|                             |   Sort Order: attention                                            |\r\n|                             | > Clear Recent Cwds: press enter/space to clear now                |\r\n|                             |     Kind: link · Scope: global                                     |\r\n|                             |     Clears the §11.7 recent-directory history (state.db's          |\r\n|                             |     recent_cwds table) immediately on enter/space -- not staged... |\r\n|                             |     not gated by ctrl+s or esc/discard, since it is a store action |\r\n|                             |     rather than a config.toml value. The history is                |\r\n|                             |     non-load-bearing: clearing it costs only the create modal's... |\r\n|                             |     prefill, up/down recent-cycling and tab completion candidates  |\r\n|      